Z||000000||FieroJET||06-21-2001||12:18 AM||||Ok here it goes.  I was driving home from work slowed down for a car turning off downshifted gased it went to shift at 5k and the engine died.  I tried to pop start it but the engine just spun.  Pushed the clutch in and tried agian.  Same result.  I pushed the clutch in and prepared to coast to the nearest road.  Then a VERY loud pop went and black smoke poured from the rear.  Towed it home thought the engine was blown.  Fiddled with it engine spun freely w/starter, No water in the oil and vise versa, but wouldn't fire.  So I pulled a spark plug out to see if it was fiering and It started!  Put the plug back in fired it up only it is now loud as hell and no exhaust is comming out of the tail pipes.  No visble leaks around the manifolds but a lot of exhaust is felt comming from the muffler area.  Test drove it everything seemed fine but the noise.  Could my muffler have clogged and caused this then blew out?  Or may I have another problem?  (No cat BTW)  I have not had time to get under the car to see the damage.  Any ideas on what to check?  <BR>Thanks for any help<BR>   JT 86 GT 4spd.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||85Josh||06-22-2001||12:47 AM||||Yup. I had a Ford Granada given to me because of this kind of thing, hacksawed the exhaust pipemin front of the cat and drove it for a year!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||06-22-2001||09:31 AM||||Hehehe Yep sure can blow one out. If you crank the engine over with the starter or by poping it, your pumping gas into the engine. it wont do anything until the air fuel ratio is just right then the hot cat converter will light it off. I dont know why it stopped running but it could have hit the rev limiter and/or the ignition (module PU coil or something) is hoakey.||||reg||1
